<h3 local-id=3D"3c63695d0613" id=3D"Rootcauseanalysis(RCA)acrossindustries:=
Commonprinciples,traditionalmethods,commercialofferingslandscapeandcasestud=
ies-5.2CriticalPath:WhatDeterminestheProjectFinishDate?">5.2 Critical Path:=
 What Determines the Project Finish Date?</h3>
<p local-id=3D"d4b8d0cd04b3">&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"a7f7b1435212"><strong>Critical Path</strong> is the longest =
sequence of dependent activities that determines the minimum time required =
to complete the project. Activities on this path have zero slack, meaning a=
 delay to any critical activity directly delays the project completion date=
. &nbsp;Slack or Float is the amount of time an activity can be delayed wit=
hout delaying the overall project completion date. Activities with positive=
 slack have some scheduling flexibility; activities with zero slack are cri=
tical.</p>
<p local-id=3D"15932a8390c8">&nbsp;</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"cb1b01e7cd18" id=3D"Rootcauseanalysis(RCA)acrossindustries:=
Commonprinciples,traditionalmethods,commercialofferingslandscapeandcasestud=
ies-5.3Supplementarydata:SuperintendentdailylogsandRFIs(Requestforinformati=
on)">5.3 Supplementary data: Superintendent daily logs and RFIs (Request fo=
r information)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"4861d60129db">Enterprise project portfolio management tools =
like Oracle P6 capture what was planned, when activities are scheduled, the=
ir logic, progress, and forecast dates; superintendent logs and RFIs provid=
e the field context explaining <em>why</em> work progressed, slowed, stoppe=
d, or changed.</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"90=
c579e5-ef10-4e80-aac5-261a76afcffe" class=3D"confluenceTable">
